              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sally"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very easily made and very tasty. This is a great way to use ham and all the cheese left over from the holiday. I agree that it could use a bit of color, so now I add a half cup OF frozen peas to the recipe."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Betsee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I did modify to use what I had, so used heavy whipping cream and queso cheese were my subs for evaporated milk and Velveeta. I also did not precook the noodles and I added minced garlic. it was good",
            "datePublished": "2021-04-06T22:36:09.897Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DizzyFarro9388"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I came across this recipe looking for a quick and easy way to use up our leftover Easter ham. No fancy ingredients required, so I was able to put it together with things I already had on hand. The recipe is easy. I added course ground salt &amp; pepper as well as some frozen peas for color. Even though we were all tired of eating ham, everyone enjoyed this flavorful casserole. If you love comfort food, this recipe is for you!",
            "datePublished": "2022-04-21T15:45:40.122Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "PamDumas"
            },
            "reviewBody": "MMMMM mmm almost the same as my tuna casserole...I didn't have cream of chicken soup so I swapped it out for cream of mushroom and I also added frozen peas for color. Instead of Velveeta I used 2 heaping tbsp of cheeze whiz and topped the whole dish up with sharp old cheddar...perfectly delicious...!!!",
            "datePublished": "2013-09-23T12:49:52.817Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kim Johnston"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I took the advice of several others and added peas, sliced mushrooms and extra ham. Next time I will use less onion, and will saute it to bring out the sweetness, as it was too strong and still a bit crunchy. I covered the casserole with aluminum foil when baking for about 40 minutes, and then removed the foil and sprinkled about half a bag of stove top stuffing, chicken flavor instead of chips on the top, baking uncovered for an additional 5 minutes...just enough time to brown the top. With the adjustments it will be worth making again.",
            "datePublished": "2025-06-18T21:54:31.238Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "FluffySpud4951"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Yes used cream of chicken and cream of celery soup. Used real cheeses and crushed crackers with butter on top. Less salty without chips and don't care for Velveeta cheese.",
            "datePublished": "2024-10-20T18:25:21.087Z"
          },
          {
